libpka (2.0-4) UNRELEASED; urgency=low

  * Give each PKA ring its own Window RAM page on kernels whose page size is
    larger than a ring's 16KB slice (e.g. 64KB-page kernels):
    - choose the Window RAM layout per platform at probe time; the driver
      passes it to pka_dev_register_shim() in the new split_window_ram
      argument (BlueField-3 only), replacing the compile-time choice
    - take each ring's window base from its own ACPI alternate window and
      fail ring initialisation if it is missing or not page aligned
    - enable PKA_SPLIT_WINDOW_RAM_MODE by default; it is only applied when
      the page size is larger than 16KB
  * Publish a ring in the shim only once it is fully initialised, and skip
    empty ring slots when a shim is released.
  * Keep a ring's Window RAM base address in a 64-bit variable so that
    addresses above 4GB are not truncated.

 -- Aiden Gula <agula@nvidia.com>  Mon, 23 Nov 2026 16:01:57 -0500

libpka (2.0-3) UNRELEASED; urgency=low

  * Fix build on RHEL 10.2 after OpenSSL ENGINE API removal (RM #5076015).
  * Add OpenSSL backend auto-selection in configure.ac:
    - build legacy ENGINE module when ENGINE API is available
    - build OpenSSL Provider module when ENGINE API is unavailable
      but Provider API exists (RHEL 10+)
  * Add provider module in engine/p_bluefield.c (X25519/X448, RSA, EC/ECDSA).
  * Update engine/Makefile.am to build libbfengine or libbfprovider.
  * Update libpka.spec for SLES %{_docdir} and RHEL 10+ provider packaging.
  * Fix doc build cleanup in doc/Makefile.am (.INTERMEDIATE html directory).
  * Fix SLES 15/16 build: %{_pkgdocdir} undefined on SLES (RM #5077628).

